Zombie Apocalypse is a game created on Twine. This story game has 6 endings the player can obtain through choosing between different dialogue options and player actions. 

The main rules for the game are:
  1. Play through the story and choose between dialogue or character action choices. 
  2. Survive as long as you can. 
  3. Collect all of the endings. 

These are the endings a player may obtain:
  1. "Good ending" 
  2. ""Why would you choose this option?" ending"
  3. "Bad ending"
  4. "Pandemic ending"
  5. "Good main ending"
  6. "Bad main ending"

How to obtain each ending: 
  1. The "Good ending"
      - The good ending gets its name because this is the ending with no casualties or sacrifices. 
    There are two ways to get this ending, 
        1) When choosing a file, choose File Three. 
            - By choosing File Three, the player will be able to choose between injecting themselves, or saying "No", and going home. By selecting the "HELL NO" option, the player is able to go home, thus completing the "Good ending". 
        2) When choosing a file, choose File One. 
            - By choosing File One, the player will be able to choose between injecting their lazy coworker, or saying "No", and going home. By selecting the "HELL NO" option, the player is able to go home, thus completing the "Good ending". 

  2. The ""Why would you choose this option?" ending"
      - This ending gets its name because out of the two options given, why would you choose the option that is a severely horrible idea?
    To obtain this ending:
        1) Choose File Three. 
            - By choosing File Three, the player will be able to choose between injecting themselves, or going home. By selecting the "inject self" option, the player goes into anaphalactic shock and dies. 

  3. The "Bad ending". 
      - This ending gets its name because the player dies in an unfortunate way. 
    The player can choose to either grab File One or File Two. However, 
        1) By grabbing File One, the player must then select the option to inject their coworker. 
            - By choosing to inject their coworker, the player will have caused the Virus to be injected in a healthy vessel to create zombies. The male coworker will then attack Anna, the female coworker. The player is then given the option to either help her or leave her. The player must choose to help her. 
            - By helping her, the player will then have to choose between caring for her wounds, or calling for help. By selecting the option "Rush to her side", the player will then be attacked by Anna, and obtain the "Bad ending". 
        2) By grabbing File Two, the player then releases an airborne pathogen onto the male coworker, turning him into a zombie. He then attacks the female coworker, Anna. The player will then be given the optoin to help Anna or leave her. 
            - By choosing to help her, the player will then have to choose between rushing to her side, or calling for help.
            - By selecting the choice "Rush to her side", the player will then be attacked by Anna, thus obtaining the "Bad ending".

  4. The "Pandemic ending". 
      - This ending get its name because after dying, the player has accidentally called many people to enter the room with the zombies. These people will then be attacked and spread the zombie apocolypse. 
    To get this ending, the player must play through until the male coworker attacks Anna. (This can be done through the steps listed above for the "Bad ending". 
      - This time however, when the player is asked to choose between "Rushing to her side' and "Call for help". Select call for help. 
      - By calling for help, the player is still attacked by Anna, but this time, after the attack, instead of being locked in one room, there will be people who respond to the scene. Those people will then be attacked and turned into zombies. They will then continue to attack and spread the zombie apocolypse to the world. 

  5. The "Good main ending". 
      - This ending gets its name as it is the main ending the game intends for players to achieve. It is good because it saves a side character that the main character is attached to. 
    To get this ending, the player must first choose to keep the hamster ball in their pocket. 
      - The player can then play through either Files One or Two. 
        1) For File One, once again, choose to inject the coworker. 
        2) For both files, the player is then given the choice to either help Anna when she is being attacked, or run and let her continue to be attacked by the male coworker. The player must choose the "Run" option. 
            - By choosing to run, the player will then be able to meet with the Janitor, who helps them lock up the zombies in the Viral Room using the hamster ball collected from the beginning. 

  6. The "Bad main ending". 
      - This ending gets its name as it is the main ending the game intends for players to achieve. It is bad however, because it saves only the main character. 
    To get this ending, the player must first choose to leave the hamster to roam free. 
      - The player can then play through either File One or File two. Once again, for file one, choosing to inject the coworker. 
        1) When Anna is being attacked by the male coworker, choose the option to "Run". 
            - By choosing to run, the player will then be able to meet with the Janitor, who helps them lock up the zombies in the Viral Room by sacrificing herself to use as bait to get the zombies into the room. 


Types of choice idioms in this game:
  - Walk through of each choice and what type of choice idiom it is:

1. Choosing a dialogue response to the female coworker asking "How has your day been?".
  - This is an example of a false choice. 
        - This is because although there are many options, all of the choices lead to the same outcome with no change in the plot. 

2. Choosing to either put the hamster ball in your pocket, or let the hamster roam free. 
  - This is an example of a delayed effect choice. 
        - This is because the player is presented with this choice at the very beginning of the game, but its consequences are not immediately shown until much later in the story. 

3. Choosing which File to take. 
  - This is an example of a blind choice. 
        - This is because the player is given no information as to what the consequences of choosing a file are. 

4. Choosing between injecting oneself or going home, and helping Anna. 
  - This is an example of a dead end choice. 
        - This is because either choice abruptly ends the game. 

5. "End", "...", and "...."
  - These are examples of unchoices. 
        - This is because they are not really choices, they are just actions to show either the end, or the passing of time. 

